   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greetings and introductions",
     "texto": [
      "«Hallo» is the usual greeting in any everyday situation, while «hoi» is more informal, between friends and young people. «Dag» works both for saying hello («good day / hello») and for saying goodbye («bye»). To introduce yourself, use «ik heet...» (my name is...) or «ik ben...» (I am...). To ask someone's name, say «Hoe heet jij?» (What is your name?). When you leave, say «tot ziens» (see you later) or «doei» (bye, informal)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
